Answer a .local host lookup as not found once it has taken 4 s

glibc's client waits 5 s for nscd's answer and, given none, stops asking
nscd for any host for its next 100 lookups, falling back to the modules
in its own process. On NixOS those can't resolve .local names, since
systemd-resolved is reached only through nscd. systemd-resolved takes
about 7 s to give up on a .local name nothing answers, so one lookup of
an absent neighbour cut a long-lived process off from every .local name
for its next hundred lookups, while fresh processes resolved them.

nsncd now answers a host lookup of a .local name as not found when it
hasn't been answered within 4 s, and leaves the lookup to finish on a
thread of its own. Other names keep waiting, since the client's own
fallback still resolves them by unicast DNS.

